{
 "id": "spool-holder-arm-pla",
 "batch": 3,
 "brief": "A filament spool holder arm in PLA (FDM, printed on its side, layers along X) that bolts to the side of a 2020 aluminium extrusion frame (the extrusion's face is the plane y = 0, 20 mm wide in X) with two M5 screws into T-nuts at x = 0, z = 10 and z = -30, through a 6 mm flange. The arm sticks out along +Y and the spool's 52 mm hole slides over it: from y = 25 to 100 the arm must fit inside a 50 mm circle centred on x = 0, z = -6 (so its top is at z = 19), and the spool rests on its top. Near the frame it stays inside x = -12 to 12, z = -40 to 19. A 1 kg spool bouncing on a moving printer puts 2 g of its weight down on the top; pulling filament off pulls 15 N sideways either way. The tip must not sag more than 1 mm, or the spool rubs the frame. Safety factor 2.",
